      <metadata>
        <description>Scripts that make REAPER faster to use with a screen reader.

Every script speaks its result through OSARA, and none of them draw their own windows, so everything stays readable by VoiceOver and NVDA.

Included:
- Automate plugin parameter by name (accessible)
- Morph between two plugin presets over the time selection (accessible)
- Ramp envelope over time selection (accessible)
- Ramp last touched parameter (accessible)
- Speak automation state (accessible)
- Find edges that could click (accessible)
- Find the loud bits (accessible)
- Line up WING-LIVE recordings (accessible)
- Make variations of selected items (accessible)
- Ripple cut with crossfades (accessible)
- Set fades on selected items (accessible)
- Speak selected items (accessible)
- Speak where the sound is (accessible)
- Insert sound by name (accessible)
- What would you like to do (accessible menu)
- Go to marker or region by name (accessible)
- Go to track by name (accessible)
- Speak what is sounding here (accessible)
- Speak project summary (accessible)
- Where does this project really end (accessible)
- Add FX by name to selected tracks (accessible)
- Build a vinyl or cassette FX chain on selected tracks (accessible)
- Create send bus from selected tracks (accessible)
- Insert track template by name (accessible)
- Rename selected tracks with a numbered pattern (accessible)
- Speak the FX chain of the selected track (accessible)
- Speak routing (accessible)

Requires OSARA. SWS is recommended.</description>
      </metadata>
